  "source": "[\\(continuous)::real.function:at{x0}]\nRefines: f\nusing: U \\:subset:/ \\reals\nwhen: x0 \"in\" U\nspecifies: f is \\function:on{U}:to{\\reals}\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: epsilon is \\real\n  where: epsilon \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n  then:\n  . exists: delta is \\real\n    suchThat:\n    . delta \\:real.greater?:/ \\real.zero\n    . forAll: x is \\real\n      where:\n      . x \"in\" U\n      . \\real.abs(x \\.real.-./ x0) \\:real.less?:/ delta\n      then: \\real.abs(f(x) \\.real.-./ f(x0)) \\:real.less?:/ epsilon\nDocumented:\n. adjective: \"continuous at $x0?$\"\n. description: \"A function is continuous at a point $x_0$ if small changes in\n                input yield arbitrarily small changes in output.\"\nId: \"0596242b-c84c-4989-a566-a5e5d1a2c884\"",
